                <pb facs="0738" n="620" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg620"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.1051/264: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-02-21T17:00:00-05:45">February 21, 1929—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:35 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>53. The guardia agreement with the amendments described in my telegram 52,
                    February 21, noon, has been signed by the President.</p>
                <p>Congress went into recess today for the purpose of studying the budget. It will
                    reconvene on March 5th for its two final sessions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
